{"h": {"measure": "R", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 112, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With e3 removed the output relies on edges 4 and 5 only, so deleting edge 5 removes a much larger share of the signal (e.g. #80 IN16 -18.9)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "If edge 5 is already absent, deleting edge 4 leaves the output fed only by edge 3, which hurts more (e.g. #36)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "When edge 4 is missing, edge 3 is one of only two inputs to the output, so removing it hurts much more (e.g. #11 IN16 -15.5)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing a missing edge 0 restores node 1's only input and all routes through it, which is a much larger gain than swapping one existing op for another (#85)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Reconnecting node 1 when edge 0 was none brings back edges 2 and 4, while replacing a conv on edge 0 with skip removes capacity (#92 vs #1, #15)."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Without the direct input-to-output edge, the route through edges 2 and 5 carries more of the signal, so cutting edge 2 hurts more (#95)."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "When edge 0 is none, edge 1 is node 2's only input, so turning it into a parameter-free pool degrades the main route (#71 C10 -20.5)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing a convolution on edge 5 with skip removes learnable capacity, while replacing none or a pool with skip is neutral or helpful (#90, #100)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Swapping the strongest op, conv3x3, for average pooling on an output edge causes a large drop (#50 -12 to -16), bigger than replacing skip or none."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a conv3x3 where the direct input-to-output edge was absent adds both a new route and capacity, so the gain should exceed that of replacing an existing op on edge 3."}], "tok": 18173, "bad": 0, "probes": [[["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1"], [0, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "none", "nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1"], [5, "none"]], [["skip_connect", "skip_connect", "none", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "none"], [0, "nor_conv_1x1"]], [["skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect", "skip_connect"], [2, "nor_conv_1x1"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "none"], [1, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["skip_connect", "none", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "none", "none"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1"], [0, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [4, "nor_conv_1x1"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "none", "nor_conv_1x1"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "none", "skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "none"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "none", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3"], [2, "none"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", 